# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repo is authored on Linux and every bash script here is sensitive to
# endings: a CRLF in scripts/zim-claude or install.sh makes the shebang
# unrunnable and the `case` patterns fail to match. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite them on checkout, so the default is
# pinned to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe's parser predates LF-only files and is unreliable with them
# (notably around labels and `goto`). Let Git hand Windows the CRLF it expects.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Windows PowerShell reads LF fine, and keeping these LF means they diff
# cleanly against their bash counterparts. Marked explicitly so a checkout on
# Windows with autocrlf=true cannot silently convert them either.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# No credential file is tracked here on purpose: the Token Juice key lives in
# ~/tokenjuice/source (mode 600, outside the repo) and install.sh never writes
# a secret into the checkout. See README.md, "Where the configuration lives".

# Screenshots are binary. Git already sniffs them and skips conversion, but
# saying so explicitly keeps a future eol rule from ever mangling an image.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
